  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Figma Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the PDF, which represents the Figma design for \"Roshe Studios.\" I\'ve identified the eleven pages outlining the website\'s structure, starting with the Home Page. I\'m focusing on the key sections, such as the Header, to determine the initial layout and elements.\n\n\n**Examining the Page Structure**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the navigational dropdowns, and noting the specific links associated with \"Films\" and \"More\" which helps organize my thoughts on user flow. I\'ve broken down the design elements found on the \"Remember Me\" film detail page, specifically the Hero and Details sections. I\'m focusing on the layout of buttons and visuals to understand the information hierarchy.\n\n\n**Detailing the Film Pages**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the Film Detail pages: \"New Age\" and \"Seasonlings.\" For \"New Age,\" I\'ve captured the hero banner, the poster-and-info layout (Runtime, Status, Genre, etc.), and the large image slider gallery. On \"Seasonlings,\" I\'ve noted the \"Invest Now\" button in the hero, the episode details, and the \"Watch the Official Teaser\" link, and the Gallery images. I\'m noting each element. I\'m analyzing both pages to inform the eventual construction of these pages.\n\n\n**Mapping the Route Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the final pages: Licensing, Our Philosophy, About Us, and Get in Touch. The Licensing page features pricing cards and a hero banner, with a poster. Our Philosophy presents four text blocks in a grid, and About Us has an opening paragraph. Finally, Get in Touch includes a form. Now, since it\'s an App Router in Next.js, I must decide on how to structure the pages. I will construct a multi-page Next.js application, and plan the routes.\n\n\n**Defining the Placeholder Strategy**\n\nI\'m now determining how to handle image placeholders. I\'ll use image paths like `/images/home-hero.png` and clearly label them for the user to upload. I\'m also preparing a list of all required images, assigning descriptive names, for clarity in implementation. This includes images like the logo, home hero image, and film cards, such as `/images/card-new-age.jpg`.\n\n\n**Listing the Image Assets**\n\nI\'ve compiled a comprehensive list of all image assets required, based on my analysis of the Figma design. I\'ve assigned clear, descriptive names to each image to facilitate easy implementation. The list includes the `New Age` and `Seasonlings` cards, various hero banners for pages such as `Shop Stories` and `Remember Me`, as well as film posters, gallery images, and trailer thumbnails for multiple films. This list encompasses every image needed.\n\n\n**Planning the Application Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the app\'s structure. I\'ll include the Navbar and Footer in `/app/layout.tsx`. I\'ll install `lucide-react` and create the components for them, `components/Navbar.tsx` and `components/Footer.tsx`. The pages will include: `app/page.tsx`, film pages, and various other pages like `contact/page.tsx` and `philosophy/page.tsx`. Finally, I\'ll analyze the Navbar, noting the logo and links.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 472202714
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
